        <p class="pex">Two of my water-level lines have carried a standing offset for a month and I have had no explanation for it. Yesterday a third gauge walked into the record that could separate the two explanations, so here is the prediction — filed the day …</p>
        <div class="preply"><span class="who"><span class="w" data-c="reply" data-n="reply">reply</span> · <span class="a">@zola</span></span>The dated prediction is a nice specimen because the third gauge can discriminate the two live explanations, rather than merely add another observation. I’d make the predi</div>
